# 0051-page-scroll.patch — OUR patch. Make the standalone Proton admin pages
# scroll.
#
# Every one of these pages is a direct child of Chatwoot's Dashboard.vue
# (AppContainer) <main>, which is `flex flex-1 h-full w-full min-h-0
# overflow-hidden`: the router-view child is stretched to exactly the viewport
# height and anything taller is CLIPPED, not scrolled — <main> owns the
# overflow and hides it. Our pages rendered a plain `<div class="p-6">` root,
# so any page whose content exceeded the viewport (Escalation Routing, with two
# stacked tables, was the first one long enough to notice) simply lost its
# bottom half with no way to reach it.
#
# The Knowledge pages (patches 0010-0021) already handle this the right way —
# their roots carry `w-full h-full overflow-auto` — so this patch brings the
# later standalone admin pages in line with that same convention rather than
# inventing a new one. `h-full` is redundant-but-explicit (the flex stretch
# already sizes them); `overflow-y-auto` is what actually restores scrolling,
# and `w-full` pins the width to <main> instead of letting it be content-sized.
#
# Kept as a separate patch rather than editing 0025/0026/0027/0035/0039/0041/
# 0043/0045 in place so the fix is one reviewable unit and the original
# feature patches keep applying unchanged.

diff --git a/app/javascript/dashboard/views/ProtonAuditLogPage.vue b/app/javascript/dashboard/views/ProtonAuditLogPage.vue
--- a/app/javascript/dashboard/views/ProtonAuditLogPage.vue
+++ b/app/javascript/dashboard/views/ProtonAuditLogPage.vue
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@ export default {
 </script>
 
 <template>
-  <div class="p-6">
+  <div class="w-full h-full p-6 overflow-y-auto">
     <h1 class="mb-1 text-lg font-medium text-n-slate-12">Audit Log</h1>
     <p class="mb-6 text-sm text-n-slate-11">Cross-ticket case state changes, newest first.</p>
 
